id: pm-vcs-p7bisect
title: Bisect stable changes using a linked pm test command
description: "Add pm vcs bisect driven by pm test <id> --run, persisting change-id results across history rewrites and restoring the original working state."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-18T03:01:48.622Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-19T17:23:32.821Z"
author: codex-agent
estimated_minutes: 480
acceptance_criteria: Good/bad boundaries identify the first failing stable change using the linked real pm test; rewritten commit ids reuse change results; interrupted/failed tests and conflicted candidates have explicit outcomes; TOON and JSON report the result and original state is restored.
parent: pm-vcs-phase7
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
  pm-vcs-p7objects,blocked_by,"2026-10-18T03:01:58.591Z",codex-agent,"cli:update:dep",detected
comments[15]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-19T12:32:18.951Z",pi-agent,"Plan for bisect: single command 'pm vcs bisect' with start|good|bad|skip|run|status|reset subcommands. Durable session state lives in the worktree's private control directory (atomic write) so a crash mid-walk leaves a resumable session; session milestones (start, conclusion, reset) are appended to PM history as comments on the linked item, so concurrent agents see each other's sessions and append-only history is never clobbered. Candidates are ordered oldest-first by ancestry; outcomes are keyed by stable change identity so rewritten commit ids (rebase/amend/describe) reuse recorded results. Linked test execution reuses the pm SDK runTest (pm test --run semantics). Outcomes: good, bad, skip (manual), untestable (spawn/timeout/signal/empty), conflicted (candidate carries unresolved conflict units). Original branch and commit are restored after success, refusal, SIGINT and crash-resume."
  "2026-10-19T13:15:08.442Z",codex-agent,"Resuming the interrupted implementation as codex-agent. Reviewing durable state, linked-test semantics, restore safety, candidate ordering and cross-agent history before completing real-repository proofs and unchanged release gates. Existing uncommitted work is preserved."
  "2026-10-19T13:24:41.877Z",codex-agent,"Review fixes: execute each candidate in a disposable native repository so tracked PM history and original checkout bytes survive test side effects, SIGINT and SIGKILL. Rebased results now map stable identities to current ancestry. Exit 125 is skip; unresolved potential culprits produce ambiguous rather than a false first_bad. Per-worktree process leases prevent concurrent local mutation; separate linked instances append start/step/halt/done/reset receipts to the shared tracker. The annotate refactor shares immutable historical harness/model provenance with the bisect report."
  "2026-10-19T13:33:56.892Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: disabling only selectBisectCandidate (returning no candidate) made both the 64-change history and rewritten-history regressions fail (0 passed, 2 failed). Restored the production function immediately. Added explicit candidate-log budget/omission reporting because the pinned PM host rejects universal read-output controls for the mixed bisect command. Long comments must be verified through full item reads; the SDK comments response abbreviates them. Public-data demo uses a locally trusted linked test, not a command inherited from a foreign Git ref."
  "2026-10-19T13:39:21.833Z",codex-agent,"Public-data proof completed: imported 34 committed public pm-csv tracker snapshots, spanning source revisions 53807ddccac4d5190deebdb52661ec398a44d0ed through 417072bd7c402f5f8d3387beb37b33d8c887ab6b. A real linked PM test identified the deliberately introduced regression at snapshot 18 (source fad7e30c040dff33f789bd6c5176882b27825427) in four executions; original checkout verified at the bad tip. Reproducer: test/bisect-demo.ts; complete TOON receipt: docs/bisect-demo.toon. Seven focused safety/CLI/legacy/budget tests pass, including SIGKILL during an active test, worker ownership refusal, unauthorized-worker refusal and resume. Annotation provenance retains its original caches; the 2000-change bounded-read regression passes."
  "2026-10-19T13:40:44.889Z",codex-agent,"The recorded linked test was executed through the pinned PM CLI with --run --only-index 1 --timeout 900 --progress: 26 tests passed, zero failed/skipped/cancelled. Full read-only annotation checks also pass, including the bounded 2000-change read proof. Core tracker authority passes with extensions disabled; normal health separately flags a pre-existing pm-github host-version skew. No dependency pins or append-only history were repaired or rewritten."
  "2026-10-19T13:56:31.357Z",codex-agent,"The full gate exposed packaging coupling: native consumers configured with **/*.toon correctly interpret every installed .toon file as a PM item, so a TOON-format report cannot use that extension. Renamed the unchanged public demo receipt to docs/bisect-demo.txt and updated its documentation link; no parser rules or tests were weakened. Reproducing both existing packed-consumer regressions after the rename."
  "2026-10-19T14:05:51.439Z",codex-agent,"Both packed-consumer regressions pass after renaming the raw TOON receipt as text (2 passed, 0 failed). The full-source inventory guard also requires its explicit expected count to increase from 67 to 70 for engine/bisect.ts, bisect-commands.ts and bisect-test-runner.ts. Updated only that count; all production globs, ignore-directive prohibition and per-file 100 percent coverage thresholds remain intact."
  "2026-10-19T14:50:13.738Z",codex-agent,"Final acceptance: npm run release:check and bun run release:check each passed 1,695/1,695 tests, zero failed/skipped/cancelled/todo. All 70 production files have per-file 100 percent statements, branches, functions and lines at unchanged thresholds (24,576 lines/statements and 848 functions; npm 7,662 branches, Bun 7,661). Both full gates used isolated HOME/Git configuration and verified copies of the indexed implementation. Final fixture-counter isolation passed the complete focused suite: 28/28. Direct installed Bun CLI bisect also found the known culprit in two linked-test executions and preserved the original checkout. Public demo: 34 distinct real tracker trees, four executions, known snapshot 18; behavioral revert: two expected regression failures. Only the PM acceptance receipt and claim-release record remain to be committed with a regenerated self-host archive. Item remains nonterminal for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-19T15:28:57.136Z",codex-agent,"Review round 1: verified the root-parent crash, HEAD manual-default mismatch, reset milestone ordering, and repeated ancestry reads. Plan: cover each behavior with revert-sensitive regressions, cache range-bounded ancestry and immutable commit reads per walk, compact report ids with --full recovery, measure demo bytes, run both release gates at unchanged coverage thresholds, refresh the self-host archive, and push without resolving review threads."
  "2026-10-19T15:34:20.409Z",codex-agent,"Round 1 regressions: root commits in unrelated merged history retain explicit and file-derived item links; all three manual outcomes target next while HEAD stays fixed; exhausted walks refuse with an explicit-revision remedy; reset removes state/workspaces before attempting its milestone and returns a warning if the item disappeared. Range decisions share cached ancestry. Scaling proof: 2,000 commits, 1,600 candidates, 2,000 setup commit reads, 10 decisions, zero additional commit reads per decision or final verdict (materialization excluded). Public demo still identifies snapshot 18 in four executions; captured TOON report shrank from 2,834 to 1,516 bytes (1,318 bytes, 46.5 percent). Default ids are 12 characters; --full retains full ids; redundant boundary revision/detail text is omitted. Six new focused regressions passed before behavioral revert checks."
  "2026-10-19T15:35:32.009Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral reverts verified independently against review head 13d39a3: linkedItems (root-parent failure), registerBisectCommands (manual HEAD mismatch, absent-candidate remedy missing, reset item-not-found failure), reportOf (64-character ids instead of 12), and each of bisectCandidates, bisectRemaining, selectBisectCandidate, bisectVerdict (read bounds exceeded). All nine targeted revert runs failed as expected; functions restored immediately after each run. The range-construction revert exceeded 2,000 reads at read 2,001; each decision-function revert exceeded the zero-additional-read bound on its first read. No review threads changed."
  "2026-10-19T15:37:34.360Z",codex-agent,"Restored implementation acceptance: pinned pm test --run --only-index 1 --timeout 900 --progress passed the complete focused suite, 34/34 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations/todo. Typecheck, build, test compilation, lint, zero-duplication and docstring checks pass. Core tracker health and validation pass with extensions disabled. Preparing the committed source and self-host snapshot for both full release gates under isolated HOME and Git configuration."
  "2026-10-19T16:47:30.738Z",codex-agent,"Release acceptance update: npm run release:check passed all 1,701 tests and every downstream gate. Bun passed 1,701 tests, all 70 production files at per-file 100 percent statements/branches/functions/lines, native TOON, stat-cache, committed self-host equality, audit, identities and packing, then correctly refused changelog verification because its verification clone was shallow. This is a clone setup error, not a package defect. Fetching complete history and tags, checking the affected tail gates, and rerunning the unmodified full Bun command. Implementation CI is green on Node 22 and 26, both Windows launcher jobs and CodeQL; no source or threshold changes are needed."
  "2026-10-19T17:23:31.423Z",codex-agent,"Final round 1 acceptance on implementation 0ff4504: npm run release:check and the full-history bun run release:check both exited zero, each with 1,701/1,701 tests and zero failed/skipped/cancelled/todo. All 70 production files have per-file 100 percent statements, branches, functions and lines at unchanged thresholds: 24,650 statements/lines, 858 functions, 7,716 branches in both final runs. Both commands passed native TOON, installed-CLI stat-cache tracing, committed self-host equality, production audit, identity audit, packaging, changelog and release attestations under isolated HOME/Git configuration. The earlier shallow-clone setup failure is corrected; the complete Bun command was rerun successfully after fetching full history and tags. Focused pinned pm linked-test run passed 34/34. Nine independent behavioral revert cases fail as expected; the final root-parent assertion was rechecked and rejects the undefined object id. Scaling: 2,000 commits, 1,600 candidates, exactly 2,000 setup commit reads and zero decision/verdict reads across 10 decisions; materialization is outside that bound. Demo: 34 public trees, four executions, snapshot 18, 2,834 to 1,516 TOON bytes (46.5 percent smaller). Fresh-clone core health and validation pass. Implementation CI is green for Node 22/26, both Windows launcher jobs and CodeQL. No new PM CLI defect or UX gap was encountered. Releasing the claim without closing the feature; final receipt and self-host snapshot will be committed and pushed, with final-head CI status recorded on PR 131. No review threads were replied to or resolved and no merge was performed."
